  <name>Oxidal</name>
  <summary>Every session in one window</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.sh4den">
    <name>sh4den</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      Oxidal puts SSH, SFTP, telnet, serial and local shells side by side in a single
      native window, organized into folders in a sidebar.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>SSH sessions with an SFTP file browser docked next to the terminal</li>
      <li>A two sided SFTP file manager with drag and drop transfers</li>
      <li>A real terminal emulator with truecolor, scroll regions and the alternate screen</li>
      <li>Live CPU, memory, network and disk monitoring for SSH hosts</li>
      <li>Serial consoles with port detection, and a proper telnet client</li>
      <li>Passwords and key passphrases kept in the system keyring, never on disk</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.sh4den.Oxidal.desktop</launchable>
  <provides>
    <binary>oxidal</binary>
  </provides>

